  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 113 PM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nLate Summer Heat Wave\nUpper-level ridging remains dominant across the Midwest this \nweek, supported by a robust nearly 600 dam 500mb high centered \nover the mid-Mississippi and Tennessee Valleys through \nWednesday. The ridge axis is progged to shift toward the Mid- \nAtlantic coast by late week. Under this subsidence, temperatures\nwill remain well above seasonal normals through the remainder \nof the week with most precipitation bypassing the local area to \nthe north, though periodic convective threats may clip central \nIllinois.\n\nSurface analysis this afternoon shows ridging along the \nAppalachians with low pressure over the Canadian Prairies, \nmaintaining a southwesterly gradient across central Illinois and\npushing ambient temperatures into the low to mid-90s. Dew point\nforecasting remains challenging as moisture advection is \ntempered by deep mixing into a very dry column. Current dew \npoints in the mid-60s to lower 70s are yielding heat indices \nnear 100 degrees.\n\nSimilar conditions are expected Tuesday and Wednesday, with an \nadditional uptick in temperatures as the 850mb thermal ridge \npeaks between 24-27C -- values exceeding the 90th percentile of\nclimatology. Surface highs will reach the mid to upper 90s, \ndriving peak heat indices into the 100-105+ range. LREF \nprobabilities for heat indices >100 degrees are high (>60%), \nfocused south of a Beardstown to Terre Haute line on Tuesday and\nexpanding south of I-74 on Wednesday. In collaboration with \nneighboring offices, the Heat Advisory was expanded to the \nremainder of the Central Illinois counties Tuesday through \nThursday.\n\nSlow Pattern Change Late Week and Weekend\nA strong shortwave trough will dig across the Great Lakes \nWednesday night and Thursday, followed by a more potent wave \nover the weekend. This will shunt the primary upper ridge axis \nback over the Great Plains, transitioning central Illinois into \na northwest flow regime. At the surface, Canadian high pressure \nbuilding across Quebec will drive a backdoor cold front through \nIllinois. This boundary will serve as the focus for slight \nchance PoPs (20%) Friday and Saturday. Temperatures will \nmoderate from the 90s ahead of the front Thursday and Friday to \nthe mid-80s in its wake for at least parts of the area Sunday. \nThe current Heat Advisory may require extension for portions of \nthe area depending on the eventual frontal speed and \nprecipitation coverage.",
